    <statement><p>Find a degree 3 polynomial whose coefficient of <m>x^3</m> equal to 1.  The zeros of
this polynomial are
<m>3</m>, <m>-4 i</m>, and <m>4 i</m>.
Simplify your answer so that it has only real numbers
as coefficients.</p>
<p>Your answer is <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(x-3\right)\mathopen{}\left(x^{2}+16\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
